Local patch for 3rd/qbe, applied after scripts/qbe-uninit-slot.patch by scripts/setup-qbe.sh.

C copies a never-initialized object of a 1-byte class (an empty lambda's storage, e.g. the _Iter_pred<lambda> that
libstdc++'s std::find_if gets in nlohmann-style code) with a direct load of its stack slot. The slot has loads and no
store, so promote() (mem.c) had no value to promote to and failed: "slot %.8 is read but never stored to". Keep the
slot instead; the loads read whatever is on the stack, as gcc's copy does. coalesce() keeps the slot through
scripts/qbe-uninit-slot.patch. Test: tests/cases/qbe_uninit_load.cpp.
--- a/mem.c
+++ b/mem.c
@@ -45,6 +45,11 @@
 			}
 			goto Skip;
 		}
+		/* nfcxx: loads and no store (C copies a never-initialized struct, e.g. an empty
+		 * lambda's 1-byte storage): there is no value to promote to. Keep the slot;
+		 * the loads read garbage, as with gcc (scripts/qbe-uninit-load.patch). */
+		if (k == -1)
+			goto Skip;
 		/* get rid of the alloc and replace uses */
 		*i = (Ins){.op = Onop};
 		t->ndef--;
